00:05:19.065 --> 00:05:22.745
Diane's question when she was tuning in here, what is affordable housing?

00:05:24.105 --> 00:05:25.705
And by the

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:27.945
Connecticut state definition,

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:34.970
affordable housing is housing that is affordable to individuals and families making 80%

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:35.850
or less

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.170
than the area median income.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:46.765
It also goes on to say that a family at that income level cannot spend more than 30% of their total income on housing,

00:05:46.925 --> 00:05:50.845
whether that's rent or mortgage taxes and insurance.

00:05:53.405 --> 00:05:59.645
Andover's median family income is about $105,000

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.390
And so what that means to us is that

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.790
if you take 80% of that

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.710
105,000,

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.390
that's about 80,000.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.710
And then if you take 30,000

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:15.475
or 30% of that to be spent on housing,

00:06:15.635 --> 00:06:17.715
it comes down to about $2,000

00:06:17.715 --> 00:06:18.515
a month.

00:06:19.315 --> 00:06:21.395
If you make less than that 80,000,

00:06:21.395 --> 00:06:25.235
obviously you've got less to spend on

00:06:25.475 --> 00:06:26.035
housing.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:31.100
Affordable housing can be rental units or private ownership,

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:34.940
and it can be condos, apartments or single family homes.

